-- title:
--   Norm string of a central idele equals its idelic norm
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an algebra over $K$, finite-dimensional over $K$ and Galois, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$, and assume `hgen`: every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$, so that $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is cyclic generated by $\sigma$. Let $w$ be a unit of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_L$ of $L$. Form the scalar matrix $\mathrm{diag}(w,w) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ ([`AutomorphicForm.centralScalar`](def/AutomorphicForm_AdelicLsXi.html#L18), i.e. `Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.scalar (Fin 2)`) and transport it entrywise through the inverse of [`AutomorphicForm.baseChangeEquiv`](def/AutomorphicForm_BaseChangePlaces.html#L65), the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ obtained by composing the commutativity isomorphism of the tensor product with [`M4aHerbrand.Bridge.genuineRingEquiv`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineTensorEquiv.html#L57), obtaining an element $\delta$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$. The assertion is that the norm string of $\delta$, namely the ordered product of the iterates $(\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})^{i}$ applied entrywise to $\delta$ for $i = 0, \dots, [L:K]-1$ ([`AutomorphicForm.normString`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L205) via [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaGL`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L202)), equals the image under the entrywise map induced by $a \mapsto 1 \otimes a$ ([`AutomorphicForm.toTensorGL`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L71)) of the scalar matrix $\mathrm{diag}(N w, N w) \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$, where $N$ is the idelic norm $\mathbb{A}_L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ of the base change [`M4aHerbrand.GenuineDescent.genuineBaseChange K L`](def/M4aHerbrand_GenuineDescent.html#L87), that is `Units.map` of the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$.
--
--   This is the norm identity for central elements underlying twisted base-change comparisons for $\mathrm{GL}_2$: entrywise it says that the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$ is the product of the conjugates $\sigma^i$ acting through $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$. It is used in the identification of twisted orbital integrals at central elements with orbital integrals of their idelic norms, and in the accompanying non-existence statement for norms of central elements modulo global points.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_normString_map_baseChangeEquiv_symm_centralScalar_eq_toTensorGL_centralScalar_idelicNorm.lean

import Definitions.Def_AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital
